## THE SEARCH RULE (PRIOR-WORK, the design question of Part 2; Q-5 of the report)
**Property.** A candidate is filed only when no existing ticket already holds the same subject, and a skipped candidate costs a named key and no write. **Rule.** Pull the whole board (`project = RD`, paged, with description, comments and labels; the drafter's pull of 20:41:26 to 20:41:31 read **954 issues, 2166 comments, 10 pages**; controls `RD-798` and `RD-923` present, a planted `@@NOPE@@zz` 0) and search LOCALLY by exact string, case-insensitive (Jira's `text ~` is stemmed). Each candidate carries one or more AND-sets of terms (THE SEARCH TABLE). A ticket COVERS a set when its summary, description and comments hold every term of the set; **you then READ the 300 characters around the first hit in each such ticket** and the candidate SKIPs only when that context states the same subject for EVERY route or file the candidate names. A ticket that holds only some terms, or covers only some of the routes, is not a skip: the candidate is FILED and names that ticket as a neighbour. Any other shape of hit (a ticket that holds all terms but speaks of another cause): prove it meets the property or FILE and name it. A finding reported with "unfiled, search: 0 hits" states the query, the frame (954 issues at drafting, re-pulled) and a control that fired. **At drafting** (all by the same program, 20:41 to 20:48): `DIALS` with `rd573` 0; `readIfPresent` 0; `clear-cache` 0; `settings/emails` 0; `setup/column-mapping` 0 hits in any ticket (the old `column-mapping` strings are in RD-42, RD-47, RD-495, RD-497, RD-832, which are about the admin route); `settings.html` with `overflow` and `390` 0 (RD-416 is a different page, 49 px, first-run); the three normalized routes together: **RD-220 and RD-231 (both To Do) hold all three and RD-187 (Done)**, read: both name the three routes and the 503s on every dashboard load, so N105B-4 is expected to SKIP; `admin.html` with `dark-mode`: **RD-167 (Testing) reads "Dark mode is a THREE-page feature: 11 of the 14 shipped pages never link dark-mode.css ... DOES NOT (11): admin.html ..."**, so N105B-3 is expected to SKIP; `/api/admin/` with open mode and `403`: 8 tickets hold the words; read: RD-618 (Release Ready) states the cause for `csp-violations` alone ("open mode sets no user ... fail-closed"), RD-832 (To Do) reports two 403 loads on admin.html with the URLs not captured, RD-497 (Release Ready) concerns the same routes registered before the auth gate, a different symptom, and RD-408 speaks of a storage fallback, so N105A-3 is a FILE naming RD-618 and RD-832.
