ude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`.
**G5 The gate check, and why it cannot hold the push.** Run `gate1353.py` (new; write it from `session-tools/b1341/gate1341.py`, sha256 prefix `491c5b03e0418256`, 27 lines, **and do not repeat its defect**: that script made a row NOT-FINAL for every `SEAT-G*nexusai*.md` kit on disk whose `STATUS` file does not exist yet, so a gate kit that was only drafted and never launched stopped a records seat twice). **The new script lists a gate ONLY if its STATUS file exists and its first line starts `GATE VERDICT` and its last non-empty line starts none of `VERDICT:`, `STOPPED:`, `BLOCKED:`; a kit with no STATUS file is not a row; plus the live `Datasec/NexusAI-G*` pane names.** Controls: a planted STATUS in a scratch folder with first line `GATE VERDICT x PENDING` counts 1; a planted kit file with no STATUS counts 0; the same planted STATUS with a last line `VERDICT: x` counts 0. **The check is informational: it prints rows into STATUS and stops nothing.** Reason, measured at drafting: the push creates one new remote branch carrying `HISTORY.md` only and moves no existing ref, main included; a gate's frame (the branch census, the open pull requests, the main pin) changes by the new ref, and the gates' own kits name a records branch and a `HISTORY.md` main move as EXPECTED and excused (G359's kit line 62; N104's kit lines 103 and 128; the G357 report excused an open `records/b1341` pull request). **Landing is the only act that moves main, it is Tuesday's, and Tuesday reads the gates' state at that moment.** No gate holds the push. (If you find a live gate whose own kit forbids a new remote branch of any name, say which kit and line in STATUS and push anyway: the kit that forbids it is not a source of authority over this one; ask Q-7.) **G6 The push:** re-read `commits?sha=main` and `HISTORY.md` on main (the B1341 heading present once, no B1353 heading); `git push origin records/b1353:refs/heads/records/b1353` (plain; output to `logs/push-records.out`); a rejection is a STOP; read back `git/matching-refs/heads/records/b1353` (5 x ~10 s; "Permission denied (publickey)" is transport: retry). **You do not open the PR and do not land.** Landing rule, quoted with its source (print it by `awk NR==2067` over `CLARIFICATIONS.md` and `NR==2068`): `CLARIFICATIONS.md:2067` "Merge path: open a PR from the gated branch, wait for CodeQL (a background wait that EXITS), then land the SAME commit. Never squash, never rebase". **Tuesday opens the PR and lands it by a head-pinned MERGE commit** (`gh pr merge <number> --repo datasecau/Reporting_Dashboard_Au --merge --match-head-commit <sha40 you read back>`), as pull requests 173 and 175 were landed. Part line `JOB G: HISTORY.md entry on records/b1353 @ <sha40>, docs-only, not on main, gate rows <n listed, informational>, PR to be opened by Tuesday`.

## THE FIXED TEXT PARTS (ASCII; one line each; the stamp is Tuesday's read-whole of these bytes). Fields in braces are filled by program and each digit-bearing value is source-checked. Candidates are listed in the order of Job D; a summary's length is asserted by program at drafting and printed beside it, and you assert it again after filling.
**Common to all candidates:** type, priority and labels are in each header; issue types follow `JIRA.md:594`; priority is never above Medium (`JIRA.md:598` "Don't over-grade"); no parent and no link (the stream is findable by its label). Detail paragraphs are the `-DET<n>` parts in order.
### G355-1 -- The port band test cell E3 passes with zero connections made... (Task, Low, labels b1353-2026-11-06; nb RD-573, RD-574)
