### G357-2 -- csp-convert.py after the CodeQL change: the end-tag pattern ... (Task, Low, labels b1353-2026-11-06; nb RD-781)
- search sets (all terms in one existing ticket; case-insensitive): {csp-convert, nbsp|\\xa0|vertical tab|\\x0b}
- `<G357-2-SUMMARY>` = csp-convert.py after the CodeQL change: the end-tag pattern also closes a script block on a vertical tab, file separator or no-break space after </script, which an HTML parser does not (summary length with the longest drafted field values: 184; limit 255)
- `<G357-2-BLUF>` = The change for RD-781 (head 030fc5476099db31fa967f0fe375b8ee75659520) writes the end tag as </script(?:[\s/][^>]*)?> at scripts/csp-convert.py line {L_CSP}. Python's \s also matches vertical tab (0x0b), file separator (0x1c) and no-break space (0xa0); the HTML tokenizer's whitespace set is tab, line feed, form feed, carriage return and space (derived from the specification, no browser run). In the tester's 78-case corpus 9 cases close a block at the head and not at the base for those three characters, beyond the forms the change names. None of the 14 shipped pages holds such a tag.
- `<G357-2-REC>` = Recommendation (a proposal, not decided): write the whitespace set out, [\t\n\f\r ], in place of \s. Low: the input is pathological and the tool is one-shot.
- `<G357-2-DET1>` = A note from the same report, not a finding: the head pattern takes quadratic time on many </script openers with no closing angle bracket (3.7 s at 8000 against 0.001 s at the base); the base was already quadratic on many unterminated script starts.
- `<G357-2-DET2>` = Source: the tester's report in the project folder, 1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-06_B1345_STATUS.md (the second finding, graded Minor, and the third, a note), made from a read of branch b1336/nexusai-devtool-alerts at head 030fc5476099db31fa967f0fe375b8ee75659520 (pull request 176, {PR176STATE}). Line numbers in this ticket are read from the files at that head by grep -n at {CLOCK} AEDT.
